A||||11||AkursedX||Intermittent Missing||||4||
Z||000000||AkursedX||06-19-2001||04:39 PM||||Ok, I seem to have a problem. (Obviously)<P>The other day, I was listening to my car run, and I revved up the throttle, and I could hear a "poot poot poot" type of sound.  It would be pretty erratic, but constant.  I can't hear it while idling, but I can hear it when I'm giving it gas.  It's not real loud though, but it sounds like one of the cylinders is missing.<P>Anyone have any ideas on the problem?  I have new plugs, wires, coil, and ignition module, but I am going to check the plugs again.  <BR>I'm thinking it might be a plugged injector, or my fuel pump is dying, but I am not really sure.<P>Thanks for any input||||reg||4
Z||000001||V8Dreamer||06-19-2001||05:00 PM||||Doubt this is your prob, but when I installed my accel coil, and some new CHEAP wires, it actually arced right through the insulation to the manifold....so if you're using a hi performance coil and a set of not so hi performance plug wires, you may want to consider that.....<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||06-19-2001||05:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by V8Dreamer:<BR><B>Doubt this is your prob, but when I installed my accel coil, and some new CHEAP wires, it actually arced right through the insulation to the manifold....so if you're using a hi performance coil and a set of not so hi performance plug wires, you may want to consider that.....<P>Ryan</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I got Splitfire 8mm wires.  Not the best, but definietly not the cheapest, but I will check for arcing this evening.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||06-19-2001||06:34 PM||||Lemme know if you find out anything...Ive got a very noticable intermitten miss in my Formula....same things have been changed as on yours. M7F||||reg||1
Z||000004||GarethWright||06-20-2001||02:07 AM||||I got so sick of my fiero doing that (among other things, such as stumbling on acceleration, light backfiring etc) that I finally gave in and took it to a mechanic *gasp* he rebuilt my distributer, reset timing and cleaned my injectors for $320, no more hesitation, poot pooting, better gas mileage too now.<BR>Definately worth the money.<BR>Good Luck with yours<BR>Gareth||||reg||1
